On Thu, 20 Oct 2005, Matt Frisch wrote:
> <claussen@dpi.physik.uni-goettingen.de> scribed into the ether:
> >Monsters are never generated in your line of sight.

When creating a monster, NetHack tries to generate it out-of-sight, but if
it fails, it may very well be generated in your line of sight. Otherwise,
some of the Big Rooms would not allow monster generation at all.

> I've had monsters generated in line of sight...not just line of sight,
> but right next to me. And no, they were not hiding under something or
> invisible or walked from a darkened corridor.

This might also happen if NetHack creates a horde of monsters; the first
one is generated in an invisible spot, the other monsters are generated
around it without a check for visibility.

